Fix EasyMesh/hwsim container boot: get_rdk_radio_indices() only returns
entries from l_radio_interface_map (built from InterfaceMap.json) whose
configured phy_index matches the *runtime-detected* phy index
(g_wifi_hal.radio_info[0].index, read from the real NL80211_ATTR_WIPHY
via netlink). On real BananaPi R4 hardware that's always phy index 0,
matching InterfaceMap.json's hardcoded "phy_index": 0 for every radio
entry, so the comparison always trivially passes there.

Inside an LXD container using mac80211_hwsim (moved in via a `physical`
nic device), the phy keeps its host-side hwsim allocation index (e.g.
40) instead of being renumbered to 0 -- confirmed the kernel refuses to
even *rename* a wiphy to "phy0" while the host's real WiFi hardware
already holds that name (EINVAL, wiphy names are unique kernel-wide,
not per network-namespace). So the comparison never matches and
map_rdk_radios_and_indexes() fails with "Failure to fetch radio map for
the phy!", and wifi_hal_init aborts before onewifi ever comes up.

FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY mode (this is the BananaPi/single-phy comment right
above this function) means there is, by construction, only ever one
phy in play -- the phy_index parameter is redundant under this mode,
since every radio entry in the config belongs to that one phy whatever
its real kernel-assigned index happens to be. Drop the comparison
instead of trying to match it.

---
 wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211_utils.c
@@ -1921,7 +1921,10 @@ int get_rdk_radio_indices(unsigned int phy_index, int *rdk_radio_indices, int
     max_radios = *num_radios_mapped;

     for (i = 0; i < get_sizeof_radio_interfaces_map(); i++) {
-        if (l_radio_interface_map[i].phy_index == phy_index) {
+        // FEATURE_SINGLE_PHY: there is only ever one phy, so every configured
+        // radio entry belongs to it regardless of its real kernel-assigned
+        // index (may not be 0, e.g. under mac80211_hwsim in a container).
+        if (1) {
             if (num_radios < max_radios) {
                 rdk_radio_indices[num_radios] = l_radio_interface_map[i].radio_index;
                 num_radios++;
